input.command:
cd /tmp && d=$(mktemp -d) && mkdir -p "$d/sub" && cat > "$d/sub/cwd.test.mjs" <<'EOF'
import { test } from 'node:test';
test('cwd probe', () => { console.log('CWD=' + process.cwd()); });
EOF
cd "$d" && node --test --test-reporter=tap sub/cwd.test.mjs | grep -E 'CWD=|# (pass|fail)' ; echo "root=$d"; rm -rf "$d"

depth.reason:
I did not stop at file presence or a green count. Checks performed:
- byte-level stdout (14 bytes; digest equal to the independently computed expected value);
- exit status, signal and timeout;
- per-file pairing from the ✔ lines for each uniquely named test;
- currentness of the CLI and both verifier dependencies against the worksite;
- protected-file identity;
- absence of package and result files;
- write territory, from the native changedPaths;
- content of all four authored assets against each original stage instruction.

